This project was originally based on telegram-signal-mcp-server by Oishh
(https://github.com/Oishh/telegram-signal-mcp-server), licensed under MIT.

The Deribit REST and WebSocket client foundations were retained from
upstream and adapted. The following modules are substantially new work
not present in upstream:

  - Cloud channel / event outbox streaming (src/event_outbox.py,
    src/events_api.py)
  - Persistent alert storage with restart survival (src/persistence.py,
    src/alerts.py rewrite)
  - Audited trading tools with pre-trade decisions (src/trading.py)
  - Daily briefings (src/briefings.py, src/briefings_api.py)
  - Market data streams and consumer lifecycle (src/market_streams.py)
  - Bifrost gateway integration and Tailscale-friendly transport
  - HTTP application layer and lifespan management (src/http_app.py,
    src/lifespan.py)
  - Scheduler and notification manager rewrite

